# The bulky binary layer of each fixture lives on the data volume
# ($HERA_DATA, default /data/sharpelab/hera-data) and is symlinked back in by
# link-data.sh — keep it out of git. Only the authored layer (frontiers/,
# ground_truth/, *.md) is tracked. A fixture is ~99.9% binary / 0.1% text.
*/data
*/images
*/runs
*/*.ipynb
# Extracted ana-notebook figures (answer-key illustrations) also live on the
# data volume and are symlinked into ground_truth/<slug>/figures — keep the
# symlink + its PNGs out of git. The authored analysis capture (method.py,
# result.md) under ground_truth/<slug>/analysis/ stays tracked.
*/ground_truth/*/figures
